## STEP 3 — write 0x5002 PoE configuration (13:51:17)
  TX 00 01 00 00 00 06 01 03 50 02 00 01   READ  0x5002 -> EXCEPTION
  TX 00 01 00 00 00 06 01 06 50 02 ff 00   WRITE 0x5002 = 0xff00 -> EXCEPTION ExceptionResponse(dev_id=1, …)
  `show power-inline` → `% Invalid input detected at '^' marker.`
  DUT log 00:52:00: "MODBUS: Request failed" / "Performed write request … port1.0.1 PoE Config
  (REG=0x5002) for 1 word with data 0xff00" / "MODBUS: Request failed".
  Server counters after: illegal data address 11 (the PoE reads/writes of this and the previous case).
Verdict step 3: UNSUPPORTED BY PLATFORM (no PoE on the IE520-28GSX).

